% c111: 273-275 Vln II plays the tune in unison with Vln I, as 41-43 (sA.ily; Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 76).
% c135: Vln II and violas restate pp at 271 under the crescendo after two bars rest (a hairpin needs a starting level; MOLA PDF 8 proofreading of the vertical; Vln I, Vc, Cb print p there)
% c272: 259 and 264 Vln II F sharp 4 (was A4): the cellos' arco A3 already carries the seventh of B7 and resolves it; the pizz. filler no longer doubles it (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 76)
dAVlnTwo = { r4 g'4\pp^\markup \italic "pizz." g'4 | r4 g'4 g'4 | r4 g'4 g'4 | r4 b4 b4 | r4 g'4 g'4 | r4 a'4 a'4 | r4 fis'4 fis'4 | R2. | r4 a'4 a'4 | r4 b'4 b'4 | r4 a'4 a'4 | r4 fis'4 fis'4 | r4 g'4 g'4 | r4 g'4 g'4 | r4 a'4 a'4 | R2. | R2. | R2. | r4 g'4\pp r4 | R2. | a''4-.\f^\markup \italic "arco" d''8-. d''-. a''4-. | c'''2->\dnb( b''8 bes''8 | a''4-.) fis''8-. fis''-. d''4-. | \transpose d b, { r4 c'4-. c'4-. } | b'2->\subP\dnb( g'4~ | g'4 e''2) | dis''2( cis''4~ | cis''4 b'4. d''8) | c''2\<->( a'4~ | a'4 fis''2) | e''2( dis''4~ | dis''4 b'4. cis''8) | b'4\f g'4( e'4) | fis'2 dis'4( | fis'4) e'2 | e'4-. r4 r4 | }
% c041: 269-270 the reprise's call is Bsn 1 solo, p staccato on E3-G3 (was Ob 1, the exposition's colour at 29): the bassoon's humorous staccato
%   (Adler I PDF 226; Ex. VII-95 Dukas, VII-96 Bartok 'Allegretto scherzando'), in its 'sweet, expressive' register (Ex. VII-89); C.a. holds the B and the
%   clarinets drop to pp so the accompanied bassoon is not swallowed (PDF 226: mark the accompaniment's dynamics).
% c017: 281-286 violas in dotted minims E-G-F sharp-E-E-C, as at 121-126 (Adler PDF 175, 179)
dAVla = { r4 b4\pp^\markup \italic "pizz." b4 | r4 b4 b4 | r4 b4 b4 | r4 fis4 fis4 | r4 b4 b4 | r4 c'4 c'4 | r4 b4 b4 | R2. | r4 c'4 c'4 | r4 b4 b4 | r4 c'4 c'4 | r4 b4 dis'4 | r4 b4 b4 | r4 b4 b4 | r4 dis'4 dis'4 | R2. | R2. | R2. | r4 b4\pp\< b4 | R2. | r4 fis'4-.\f^\markup \italic "arco" fis'4-. | r4 fis'4-. fis'4-. | r4 fis'4-. fis'4-. | \transpose d b, { r4 fis4-. fis4-. } | e'2.\subP( | g'2.) | fis'2.~( | fis'4 g'2) | e'2.\<( | c'2.) | b2--( b4--~ | b4 e'2) | e'4\f e'--( e'--) | dis'2 b4 | b2. | b4-. r4 r4 | }
% c071: 281-287 the second idea's last statement adds a tenor octave in Hn 2 and the cellos (C4-A3-F sharp 4 ..., an octave under Vln II and Ob 1):
%   Adler II PDF 27 (ch. 11, 'usually the horn and cello double on long sustained melodies', Strauss Ex. XI-10); PDF 20 (Hindemith: a later
%   statement of the theme takes a colour saved for it). The basses keep Cb, Bsn 2 and Cbsn; Hn 2 leaves its pad (Hn 1, Cl 1, violas keep the harmony).
dAVc = { b2.~\pp^\markup \italic "arco, sostenuto" | b2.( | g2. | fis2.) | g2.( | e2. | a2. | g2.) | e2.( | b2. | c'2. | a2.) | g2.( | b2. | a2. | g2) r4 | R2. | R2. | e,4\p\<^\markup \italic "pizz." r4 r4 | b,4 r4 r4 | d4\f r4 r4 | d4 r4 r4 | d4 r4 r4 | R2. | e,2(\subP^\markup \italic "arco" g,4~ | g,4 e,2) | b,2( a,4~ | a,4 g,2) | c'2->\<( a4~ | a4 fis'2) | e'2( dis'4~ | dis'4 b4. cis'8) | b4\f g4( e4) | fis2 dis4( | fis4) e2 | e4-. r4 r4 | }
